.git
.claude
# What a Dockerfile `COPY . .` must never carry into a layer (p6-ops): the secret files (the root directory and any directory of the
# name below the tree), the signed node bundles, the host's .env and its backups, and the NTS keys of chrony. All of them are
# gitignored, so no review would ever see one in a layer. deploy/compose/.env.example stays: the Go image embeds the compose file
# beside it.
secrets
**/secrets
deploy/bundles
deploy/compose/.env
deploy/compose/.env.bak*
deploy/chrony/nts
**/node_modules
**/.next
*.exe
*.test
*.out
deploy/compose/.env
docs
.codegraph
apps
packages
content
tools/web-lint
pnpm-lock.yaml
pnpm-workspace.yaml
package.json
tsconfig.base.json
eslint.config.mjs
.npmrc
